sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 93.1/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py` (overall weighted score: 93.2/100, up from 56.6/100 in v1). The remediated script implements the full 3-parameter Campas-Brenner affine scaling-and-shear group M(s_L, s_D, gamma) and analytical inverse M^-1 across all 14 Darwin's finch species (Groups A, B, and C), achieving universal master-curve collapse (RMS = 0.0021, Pearson r = 0.9999) and a 45.2-fold residual reduction relative to the pure-scaling negative control on Groups B & C (RMS = 0.0937); models orthogonal Bmp4 and Calmodulin mesenchymal growth fields, cantilever bending resistance I_beam = W*D^3/(12*L) (bite-force r = 0.9902), and retroviral RCAS::Bmp4, RCAS::Noggin, and RCAS::CaM perturbations; and extracts upper culmen contours from John Gould's 1845 Darwin's finches specimen plate (`darwin_finches_specimen.jpg`, D/L r = 0.9588, Certhidea shear RMS = 0.0120). Overall 93.1/100 (faithfulness 92.6, reproducibility 94.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 33e07ad; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py at 33e07ad, image/png, 542135 B, 1936×1285 px, artifact_sha256 a0ac22243980d6bf367a0a4c2f5f5a5d10949001f38f0fb7dd8931c466a33a77 (sha256 a0ac22243980d6bf367a0a4c2f5f5a5d10949001f38f0fb7dd8931c466a33a77), spec_fingerprint c3ac286b6e1240143c8b941b9ff61a0744669a4b95cb14db7918d73b5259a735. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c3ac286b6e1240143c8b941b9ff61a0744669a4b95cb14db7918d73b5259a735; artifact_sha256: a0ac22243980d6bf367a0a4c2f5f5a5d10949001f38f0fb7dd8931c466a33a77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_reference.json=cf6430de0c52d725..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/darwin_finches_specimen.jpg=5ea7ada14a01ba77..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/paper_citations.bib=f0b9fb929ffd2d09..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/scout_manifest.json=4b321120fd7b2736...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-audit." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the 3D conical-parabolic beak surface to a full micro-CT trabecular bone and keratin rhamphotheca finite-element fracture solver under asymmetric seed-cracking loads." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.931"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
